{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nst=json.load(open('../state.json'))\nrec=[i for i in st['interpretations'] if i.get('id')=='69ed488d46854e82ac7202fb04ae501e-interpretation-0'][0]\n\nlim=[l for l in rec['limitations'] if not l.startswith('The stale-read consequence')]\nnew_lim=(\\\"The stale-read consequence needs a successor elected while the old leader reports verify success, and the two orderings that decide it are both in the source. A voter refuses a vote or a pre-vote while it still knows a leader other than the candidate (raft.go 1673-1679 and 1786-1792), and it clears that knowledge only in its own campaign path, which runs after HeartbeatTimeout without leader contact (raft.go 227-228). A successor therefore needs a quorum of voters that have already reached that trigger, so it cannot exist earlier than HeartbeatTimeout after their last contact with the old leader, plus the election rounds. The leader, meanwhile, steps down at the first lease check whose voter contact age exceeds LeaderLeaseTimeout, and ValidateConfig allows LeaderLeaseTimeout to equal HeartbeatTimeout: in the worst schedule the boundary check still counts the voter (the comparison is diff <= leaseTimeout) and the step-down follows after minCheckInterval = 10ms. So under a validated configuration the leader leaves office in at most LeaderLeaseTimeout + 10ms, which is at most HeartbeatTimeout + 10ms, while no successor can be elected before HeartbeatTimeout plus a round of pre-vote and vote. The residual exposure is therefore confined to configurations with LeaderLeaseTimeout == HeartbeatTimeout and schedules where the granters clear at the earliest instant, and it is a few milliseconds at most; the practical route to a longer exposure is a leader whose own goroutine is stalled or whose clock jumps, which the earlier account relied on.\\\")\ninterp={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"3b823834c8cb46da98e77d8e988bf5d9-question-0\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":list(dict.fromkeys(rec['source_ids']+[\\\"vote_leader_known_check\\\",\\\"prevote_leader_known_check\\\",\\\"follower_clears_leader\\\"])),\n \\\"executions\\\":rec['executions'],\n \\\"conclusion\\\":rec['conclusion'],\n \\\"defect_claim\\\":rec['defect_claim'],\n \\\"rationale\\\":rec['rationale'],\n \\\"knowledge\\\":rec['knowledge'],\n \\\"answers\\\":{\\\"d704b04e706144dc964ff451359eda19-gap-0\\\":{\n   \\\"explanation\\\":(\\\"Still unresolved, but now bounded from both sides. The grant side closes what the previous answer left open: a voter rejects a vote request while it still knows a leader other than the candidate (raft.go 1673-1679, and the same check on pre-votes at 1786-1792) and clears that knowledge only when its own campaign path runs, which requires HeartbeatTimeout without leader contact (raft.go 227-228). A successor therefore needs a quorum of voters past that trigger, so the earliest successor is HeartbeatTimeout plus the election rounds after the last contact, while the old leader steps down at the first lease check with voter contact age exceeding LeaderLeaseTimeout, at the latest LeaderLeaseTimeout + minCheckInterval (10ms) <= HeartbeatTimeout + 10ms. With the documented defaults the leadership window closes about 500ms before any successor can exist; only an equal-lease configuration leaves a residual of a few milliseconds, and that needs the granters to clear at the earliest instant. What remains untested is whether that residual is reachable at all, and whether a stalled leader goroutine widens it, so the gap stays open as a schedule-dependent condition rather than a configuration-dependent one.\\\"),\n   \\\"resolved\\\":False}},\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":rec['counterevidence']+[\n   \\\"The grant side bounds the consequence more tightly than the verify quorum does: because a voter refuses votes while it knows another leader, no successor can be elected before HeartbeatTimeout plus an election round after the last leader contact, while the lease removes the old leader at LeaderLeaseTimeout + minCheckInterval at the latest; with the documented defaults the two cannot overlap, and even when LeaderLeaseTimeout equals HeartbeatTimeout the residual is a few milliseconds.\\\"],\n \\\"limitations\\\":[new_lim]+lim}\n\nd={\\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Tightened the verify question's consequence in the honest direction. The previous limitation treated the boundary schedule (LeaderLeaseTimeout == HeartbeatTimeout with the 10ms check floor) as an open route of about 10ms plus the election; reading the grant side shows the election cannot be that fast, because a voter refuses votes while it still knows another leader and only clears that in its own campaign path after HeartbeatTimeout without contact. So no successor can exist before HeartbeatTimeout plus an election round, while the old leader leaves office by LeaderLeaseTimeout + 10ms <= HeartbeatTimeout + 10ms, which makes the overlap a few-millisecond residual at most and adds a concrete item to the counterevidence. The gap answer and limitation now record that bound; the question's evidence, executions and defect claim are unchanged.\\\"),\n \\\"sources\\\":[\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"vote_leader_known_check\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1673,\\\"end_line\\\":1679,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"prevote_leader_known_check\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1786,\\\"end_line\\\":1792,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n  {\\\"id\\\":\\\"follower_clears_leader\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":225,\\\"end_line\\\":241,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[interp]}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
